#: include/admin-interfaces/security-scan/scan_item_headers.php:29
msgid "HTTP Response Security Headers"
msgstr "HTTP-respons-sikkerhetsheadere"

#: include/admin-interfaces/security-scan/scan_item_headers.php:32
msgid ""
"HTTP Response Headers are a powerful tool to Harden Your Website.\n"
"                                                                The Hypertext Transfer Protocol (HTTP) is based on a client-server architecture, in which the client ( typically a web browser application ) establishes a connection with the server through a destination URL and waits for a response.\n"
"                                                                The HTTP Headers allow the client and the server send additional pieces of information with the HTTP request or response.\n"
"                                                                The HTTP Headers are categorised by their purpose: Authentication, Caching, Client hints, Conditionals, Connection management, Content negotiation, Controls, Cookies, CORS, Downloads, Message body information, Proxies, Redirects, Request context, Response context, Range requests, Security, Server-sent events, Transfer coding, WebSockets, Other\n"
"                                                                This area provides support for the <a href='https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers#security' target='_blank'>Security Headers</a> type. Those are the ones responsible for the security implementation for any page."
msgstr ""
"HTTP-respons-headere er et kraftig verktøy for å styrke nettstedet ditt.\n"
"                                                                Hypertext Transfer Protocol (HTTP) er basert på en klient-server-arkitektur, der klienten (vanligvis en nettleserapplikasjon) etablerer en tilkobling med serveren gjennom en destinasjons-URL og venter på et svar.\n"
"                                                                HTTP-headere tillater klienten og serveren å sende ekstra informasjonsbiter med HTTP-forespørselen eller responsen.\n"
"                                                                HTTP-headere kategoriseres etter deres formål: Autentisering, Hurtiglager, Klienthints, Betingelser, Tilkoblingshåndtering, Innholdsforhandling, Kontroller, Informasjonskapsler, CORS, Nedlastinger, Meldingstekstinformasjon, Proxies, Omdirigeringer, Forespørselskontekst, Responskontekst, Rekkeviddeforespørsler, Sikkerhet, Server-sendte hendelser, Overføringskoding, WebSockets, Annet\n"
"                                                                Dette området gir støtte for <a href='https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers#security' target='_blank'>Sikkerhetsheadere</a>-typen. Disse er ansvarlige for sikkerhetsimplementeringen for enhver side."

#: include/admin-interfaces/security-scan/scan_item_headers.php:86
msgid "<span class=\"dashicons dashicons-no\"></span>Your site is missing some security headers."
msgstr "<span class=\"dashicons dashicons-no\"></span>Nettstedet ditt mangler noen sikkerhetsheadere."

