"Using the option the system try to misguide the used WordPress by outputting the wrong traces, of the selected CMS.\n"
"                                                                <br />Misleading and making a false lead provides an extra security, as the attacker search and attempt to hack something which not exist."
msgstr ""
"Ved å bruke alternativet prøver systemet å villede den brukte WordPress ved å sende ut feil spor, fra den valgte CMS-en.\n"
"                                                                <br />Villedende og å lage en falsk ledetråd gir ekstra sikkerhet, ettersom angriperen søker og prøver å hacke noe som ikke eksisterer."

#: include/admin-interfaces/security-scan/scan_item_hide_emulate.php:55
msgid "<span class=\"dashicons dashicons-no\"></span>It's recommended to use the option to output specific CMSs HTML traces to mislead any peculiar check."
msgstr "<span class=\"dashicons dashicons-no\"></span>Det anbefales å bruke alternativet for å sende ut spesifikke CMS HTML-spor for å villede enhver spesiell sjekk."

#: include/admin-interfaces/security-scan/scan_item_hide_json.php:29
msgid "JSON REST"
msgstr "JSON REST"

#: include/admin-interfaces/security-scan/scan_item_hide_json.php:32
msgid ""
"The WordPress REST API is an easy-to-use set of HTTP endpoints which allows access a site data in simple JSON format. That including users, posts, taxonomies and more. Retrieving or updating is as simple as sending a HTTP request.\n"
"                                                                <br />A REST API can be consumed everywhere. On mobile applications, on front-end (web apps) or any other devices that have access on the net, practically everything can connect from anywhere to your site and interact though JSON REST API service."
msgstr ""
"WordPress REST API er et enkelt å bruke sett med HTTP-endepunkter som gir tilgang til nettstedsdata i enkelt JSON-format. Det inkluderer brukere, innlegg, taksonomier og mer. Henting eller oppdatering er like enkelt som å sende en HTTP-forespørsel.\n"
"                                                                <br />En REST API kan konsumeres overalt. På mobilapplikasjoner, på front-end (web-apper) eller enhver annen enhet som har tilgang til nettet, kan praktisk talt alt koble til fra hvor som helst til nettstedet ditt og samhandle gjennom JSON REST API-tjeneste."

#: include/admin-interfaces/security-scan/scan_item_hide_json.php:58
msgid "<span class=\"dashicons dashicons-no\"></span>The JSON endpoint should be customised. If not used, should be disabled."
msgstr "<span class=\"dashicons dashicons-no\"></span>JSON-endepunktet bør tilpasses. Hvis det ikke brukes, bør det deaktiveres."

#: include/admin-interfaces/security-scan/scan_item_hide_json_clean_api.php:29 modules/components/rewrite-json-rest.php:146 modules/components/rewrite-json-rest.php:150
msgid "Clean the REST API response"
msgstr "Rens REST API-responsen"

#: include/admin-interfaces/security-scan/scan_item_hide_json_clean_api.php:32
msgid ""
"When calling the site REST API base route ( e.g. /wp-json/ or ?rest_route=/ ) the service outputs all available namespaces and routes for current site. This can be a breach for the system, as outputs important information regarding certain used theme and plugins.\n"
"                                                                <br />Recommended selection for this option is Yes, to ensure no inside data is being exposed. "
msgstr ""
"Når du kaller nettstedets REST API-baserute (f.eks. /wp-json/ eller ?rest_route=/) sender tjenesten ut alle tilgjengelige navnerom og ruter for gjeldende nettsted. Dette kan være et brudd for systemet, ettersom det sender ut viktig informasjon om visse brukte temaer og plugins.\n"
"                                                                <br />Anbefalt valg for dette alternativet er Ja, for å sikre at ingen interne data eksponeres."

#: include/admin-interfaces/security-scan/scan_item_hide_json_clean_api.php:55
msgid "<span class=\"dashicons dashicons-no\"></span>The \"Clean the REST API response\" should be active."
msgstr "<span class=\"dashicons dashicons-no\"></span>\"Rens REST API-responsen\" bør være aktiv."

#: include/admin-interfaces/security-scan/scan_item_hide_license_txt.php:29 modules/components/rewrite-root-files.php:117 modules/components/rewrite-root-files.php:121
msgid "Block license.txt"
msgstr "Blokker license.txt"

#: include/admin-interfaces/security-scan/scan_item_hide_license_txt.php:32 modules/components/rewrite-root-files.php:122
msgid "This is a text file which contain the licensing terms for WordPress framework. Obviously you don't want that visible as every site containing such file must be a WordPress."
msgstr "Dette er en tekstfil som inneholder lisensvilkårene for WordPress-rammeverket. Åpenbart vil du ikke at dette skal være synlig, ettersom hvert nettsted som inneholder en slik fil må være en WordPress."

#: include/admin-interfaces/security-scan/scan_item_hide_license_txt.php:54
msgid "<span class=\"dashicons dashicons-no\"></span>The license.txt file is still accessible."
msgstr "<span class=\"dashicons dashicons-no\"></span>license.txt-filen er fortsatt tilgjengelig."

#: include/admin-interfaces/security-scan/scan_item_hide_new_wp_login.php:29 modules/components/admin-login_php.php:98 modules/components/admin-login_php.php:102
msgid "New wp-login.php"
msgstr "Ny wp-login.php"

#: include/admin-interfaces/security-scan/scan_item_hide_new_wp_login.php:32
msgid ""
"There are a lot of security issues that come from having your login page open to the public. Most specifically, brute force attacks. Because of the ubiquity of WordPress, these kinds of attacks are becoming more and more common.\n"
"                                                                <br />Map a new wp-login.php instead default prevent hackers boot to attempt to brute force a site login. Being known only by the site owner, the url itself becomes private."
msgstr ""
"Det er mange sikkerhetsproblemer som kommer av å ha innloggingssiden din åpen for offentligheten. Mest spesifikt, brute force-angrep. På grunn av WordPress's utbredelse, blir slike angrep mer og mer vanlige.\n"
"                                                                <br />Kartlegg en ny wp-login.php i stedet for standard for å forhindre hackere i å forsøke brute force på en nettstedinnlogging. Ved å være kjent kun av nettstedeieren, blir URL-en selv privat."

#: include/admin-interfaces/security-scan/scan_item_hide_new_wp_login.php:55
msgid "<span class=\"dashicons dashicons-no\"></span>Map a new wp-login.php instead default prevent hackers boot to attempt to brute force a site login. Being known only by the site owner, the url itself becomes private."
msgstr "<span class=\"dashicons dashicons-no\"></span>Kartlegg en ny wp-login.php i stedet for standard for å forhindre hackere i å forsøke brute force på en nettstedinnlogging. Ved å være kjent kun av nettstedeieren, blir URL-en selv privat."

#: include/admin-interfaces/security-scan/scan_item_hide_other_generator.php:29 modules/components/general-meta.php:177 modules/components/general-meta.php:181
